@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-top-layer`
IMPORT `retl-9-purchase-tax`

-- Tests for the Real Estate Taxation Law s 9 (the purchase tax on a residential apartment). Every expected value was worked by hand from the printed bands
-- (the arithmetic is beside each group) before it was run. A failing assertion is a finding. All values are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 9`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      value IS A NUMBER
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      only  IS A BOOLEAN
      sold  IS A BOOLEAN
      group IS A BOOLEAN
      repl  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment`
`a purchase on` day `of a right worth` value `, resident individual` resident `, only apartment` only `, sold the other` sold `, purchase-group case` group `, replacement` repl MEANS
    `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment` WITH
        `the day of the sale` IS day
        `the value of the right sold` IS value
        `the buyer is an individual resident in Israel` IS resident
        `the apartment is the buyer's only apartment` IS only
        `the buyer sold the other apartment that was his only one within the period` IS sold
        `the buyer bought the apartment after a purchase-group apartment was delayed, as (c1c)(2)(b1) says` IS group
        `the apartment is a replacement apartment as section 49E(a) means` IS repl

`no index readings` MEANS NOTHING

GIVEN new IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)`
`index readings` new `over` base MEANS
    `Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)` WITH
        `the new index, last published before the update day` IS new
        `the base index, published on 15 January 2027` IS base

`the default 1` MEANS `declined where the end of the period changes the answer`
`the default 2` MEANS `declined where the rounding of a half changes the answer`

§§ `Paragraph (c1c)(2): who pays by the bands of (3)`
#ASSERT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE)
#ASSERT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` TRUE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE)
#ASSERT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` TRUE `, replacement` FALSE)
#ASSERT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` TRUE)
-- None of the four: no. Not a resident individual: no, though it is his only apartment.
#ASSERT NOT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `retl 9(c1c)(2) — the buyer pays by the bands of paragraph (3) for` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` FALSE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE)

§§ `The bands of (c1c)(2)(3) (printed for 2025)`
-- 2,000,000: 0% up to 1,978,745 ; 3.5% on 21,255 = 743.925.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 743.925
-- Exactly 1,978,745: 0.  One shekel more: 3.5% of 1 = 0.035.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 1_978_745 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 1_978_746 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 0.035
-- 7,000,000: 3.5% x 368,295 (12,890.325) + 5% x 3,708,030 (185,401.5) + 8% x 944,930 (75,594.4) = 273,886.225.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 7_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 273_886.225

§§ `The bands of (c1c)(1) and of (c1f) (printed for 2025); fork P1`
-- An investor (none of the four), 2,000,000: (c1c)(1): 5% x 1,465,800 (73,290) + 6% x 534,200 (32,052) = 105,342 ; (c1f): 8% x 2,000,000 = 160,000.
--   On 30 June 2026 the (c1f) period has run (if it ends in 2026) or has not (if it ends in 2024): the readings part. On 1 January 2027 both give 105,342.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the period ends on 31 December 2024, as the paragraph prints it` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 105_342
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the period ends on 31 December 2026, as the consolidation's note on the extension says` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 160_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` BECAUSE "section 9(c1f) is printed as ending on 31 December 2024 and the consolidation's note says it was extended to 31 December 2026 by an order that is not deposited, and here the end of the period changes the answer"
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 105_342
-- The last day of the extended period, 31 December 2026: the readings still part.  The first day of the table, 16 January 2025: answered on a named reading.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` BECAUSE "section 9(c1f) is printed as ending on 31 December 2024 and the consolidation's note says it was extended to 31 December 2026 by an order that is not deposited, and here the end of the period changes the answer"
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2025 1 16) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the period ends on 31 December 2024, as the paragraph prints it` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 105_342
-- 25,000,000 after the period on every reading (1 February 2027), (c1c)(1): 73,290 + 6% x 2,931,580 (175,894.8) + 7% x 1,657,690 (116,038.3) + 8% x 14,128,495 (1,130,279.6) + 10% x 4,816,435 (481,643.5) = 1,977,146.2.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2027 2 1) `of a right worth` 25_000_000 `, resident individual` FALSE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 1_977_146.2

§§ `The dates`
-- Before 16 January 2025: declined.  15 January 2028 is the last day of the printed amounts: answered.  16 January 2028: the index readings are needed.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2025 1 15) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` BECAUSE "the bands of section 9(c1c) are printed for the tax years 2025 to 2027 only, and for an earlier sale the amounts are indexed from base months whose indices are not supplied"
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2028 1 15) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 743.925
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2028 1 16) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` TRUE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` `no index readings` `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` BECAUSE "from 16 January 2028 section 9(c2) adjusts the amounts by the housing-services index, and the readings were not supplied"

§§ `Paragraph (c2): the amounts adjusted by the index and rounded to a multiple of 5`
-- Index 105 over a base of 100 (a rise of 5%): 1,465,800 x 1.05 = 1,539,090 (a multiple of 5) ; 4,397,380 x 1.05 = 4,617,249 -> 4,617,250 ; 6,055,070 x 1.05 = 6,357,823.5 -> 6,357,825 ;
-- 20,183,565 x 1.05 = 21,192,743.25 -> 21,192,745.
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 1_465_800 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 105 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 1_539_090
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 4_397_380 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 105 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 4_617_250
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 6_055_070 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 105 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 6_357_825
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 20_183_565 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 105 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 21_192_745
-- A half: 1,000 x 100.25 / 100 = 1,002.5, which is half way between 1,000 and 1,005: up 1,005 ; down 1,000 ; refused by default.
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 1_000 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 100.25 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `a half goes up` EQUALS 1_005
#ASSERT `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 1_000 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 100.25 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `a half goes down` EQUALS 1_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 9(c2) — the amount` 1_000 `adjusted by` (`index readings` 100.25 `over` 100) `and rounded to a multiple of 5, reading a half as` `declined where the rounding of a half changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 9(c2) rounds to the nearest multiple of 5 shillings and does not say where a half goes, and here it changes the answer"
-- 16 January 2028, index 105 over 100, an investor (the (c1f) period over): bands adjusted to 1,539,090 (5%), then 6%: 5% x 1,539,090 (76,954.5) + 6% x 460,910 (27,654.6) = 104,609.1 on 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `retl 9 — the purchase tax on` (`a purchase on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `of a right worth` 2_000_000 `, resident individual` TRUE `, only apartment` FALSE `, sold the other` FALSE `, purchase-group case` FALSE `, replacement` FALSE) `, the index readings being` (JUST (`index readings` 105 `over` 100)) `, reading the end of (c1f) as` `the default 1` `and the rounding of a half as` `the default 2` EQUALS 104_609.1
